WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:01.550
- "My 600-lb Life".

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:02.810
I'm curious how it compares

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.080
to the other show that we've
watched, "Family by the Ton."

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.200
Hate the names of these shows,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.290
but let's see what it's got.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.490
Huge thank you to ZipRecruiter

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.430
for sponsoring this video, bewoop.

00:00:11.855 --> 00:00:14.208
- One, two, one, two, three.

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:16.540
(gentle music)

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.800
- Repositioning is of utmost importance,

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.540
especially when you're
overweight to this degree

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.180
because you start putting pressure

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.750
on certain areas of your skin,
your muscles, your bones.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.380
You could develop pressure ulcers.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.080
Those can get infected,

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.310
becomes very, very complicated to treat.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.503
- I have no life.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.020
My legs can't even hold my weight anymore.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.170
- That's why it's so important

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.710
when we talk about someone
being obese or being overweight,

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.280
we talk about their quality of life

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.160
being equally as important
as their state of health

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.010
and their risks that they face.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.243
- My weight has condemned me to this bed.

00:00:52.595 --> 00:00:54.033
I can't do anything.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.680
I can't even bathe myself.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.020
- It's really important that you clean

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.460
within the skin folds as well

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.130
'cause bacteria can get trapped there.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.510
It's a dark, moist
environment most of the time,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.090
and as a result, fungi thrive
in that type of environment.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.080
So not only do you have to wash it well,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.510
but you have to dry it well as well.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:14.510
- I have arthritis, gout,
lymphedema, diabetes.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.780
- I wouldn't be surprised

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.880
if this is all a result
of metabolic syndrome,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.010
which can develop from being
overweight to this degree.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.990
You know, a lot of people,

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.970
when I even talked about bariatric surgery

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.420
on some of my past videos

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.150
were quite critical of me for saying that,

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.400
that bariatric surgery can
be an option for somebody.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.250
But for somebody like this who
is struggling to move around

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.083
because of arthritis,

00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:34.740
because of legitimate medical conditions,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.280
she's unable to take care
of herself on her own.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.890
So yes, bariatric surgery
can be a life changer,

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.690
a life saver in many cases.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:43.680
While I don't think it's
appropriate in all cases,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.900
far from all cases,

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.230
I think you need to be
open-minded that in medicine,

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.710
the selection for the treatment

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.700
depends on the individual
patient in front of you,

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:52.770
and this patient for now,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.345
at least it makes sense.

00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:55.790
(somber music)

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.103
- As a kid, I was never overweight.

00:02:00.593 --> 00:02:01.990
(somber music)

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.820
It wasn't until my early 20s

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.153
that my weight started to be a problem.

00:02:09.381 --> 00:02:10.360
(somber music)

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.750
I tried to break up with
my boyfriend at the time.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.313
He lost it, and he took me hostage.

00:02:18.986 --> 00:02:20.300
(somber music)

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.510
He held me a gun point

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.170
and I thought I was gonna die.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.110
- A lot of folks rush to judge people.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:30.980
Many feel like fat shaming is appropriate

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.980
because they view someone
who is obese as lazy.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.180
People have true problems,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.710
medically related and
psychologically related.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.710
This person dealt with
a traumatic situation

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.580
and perhaps that is the cause

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.090
of the start of this condition.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.570
So to judge someone unfairly

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.370
just by simply writing
them off as lazy is unfair,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.520
and that's why we're against
fat shaming on this channel.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.900
- I was too scared to leave the house,

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.393
and I lived in constant fear,

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.173
and I just ate.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:01.710
I'm a junk food junkie.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.690
- A lot of times when you
eat those types of foods,

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.490
they can increase temporarily

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.990
some neurotransmitters in your brain

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:07.970
that help you feel good.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.990
So it almost becomes a
type of self medication

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.650
when you start binging foods like that,

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.100
especially the junk foods.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.120
- If she don't lose the weight,

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.410
I'm afraid this shall pass.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.680
- It's a very reasonable concern to have

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.100
when someone is of that size

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.430
'cause you're putting tremendous strain

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.410
on your every organ in your body,

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.730
and it's an unnatural strain as well.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.470
- We're expecting
arrival of Marla McCants.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.740
From what I understand,

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.583
she may be close to 800 pounds.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.130
If she's that big,

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.610
and she should have
used bariatric ambulance

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.350
with medical care to go with her.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.830
She should not have come
to Houston on her own.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.280
She should have waited for a safer option.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.200
- Yeah, I agree, but at the same time

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.700
that safer option may be
unaffordable to most people.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.990
That's why, as a doctor,

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.740
you can't just make recommendations.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.380
You have to make recommendations
with the patient in mind.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.410
Do they wanna do this?

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.670
Can they afford to do this?

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.640
Is this service even available to them?

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.500
- I can already see that she is in

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.390
one of the worst condition
health-wise I ever seen.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.790
- For a prolonged trip like
that with lack of mobility,

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.730
her chance of developing a blood
clot goes through the roof,

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.890
and why is that dangerous?

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.710
Because a blood clot is
more likely to happen

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:17.880
in the lower extremities,

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.670
and if that clot travels
in the circulation back

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.350
to the heart and then to the lungs,

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.200
and gets stuck there,

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.890
you develop a pulmonary embolism

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.010
which cuts off blood supply to the lung,

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.000
and essentially, that part
of the lung starts dying.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.155
You could see how that
could quickly become fatal.

00:04:31.155 --> 00:04:33.070
- I can't move my legs.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:34.520
- Your leg hurt?

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.478
(Marla groans)

00:04:35.478 --> 00:04:37.900
(somber music)

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.180
Look, it got that a
little bit swelling, huh?

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.730
- Well, that swelling could
be as a result of the DVT,

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.150
that clot we just talked about,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.170
or it could be her lymphedema acting up.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:47.440
- We're gonna run some tests

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.700
to find out what maybe going on with you.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.790
- The test that they're usually
running in these situations

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.210
would be a Doppler ultrasound
of the lower extremities,

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.350
which is an ultrasound
to check for blood flow

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.500
in the lower extremities to
see if everything's opened,

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.810
if all the blood vessels are open,

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.850
and then also a D-dimer test.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.080
And sometimes if they suspect

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.090
that the clot is already
traveled to the lungs,

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:08.040
we can do a special type of CAT scan.

